WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.709 --> 00:00:06.339
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, hopefully you’ve
all had a chance to see the premiere of Star

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.339
Wars Rebels.

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:09.790
This video is going to be my top 10 moments.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:13.730
Disney was really nice and made the episode
available early on the Disney XD website,

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:17.990
so I already did a review that I’ll link
in the description.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.710
But I didn’t include any spoilers.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:30.980
So careful if you haven’t seen it but let’s
dig into this...I’ll wait just a sec...okay.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.790
Here we go.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:39.690
Number 10 - The Star Destroyer Intro

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:43.949
Thematically I feel like every new Star Wars
video related project has to begin with an

00:00:43.949 --> 00:00:45.399
overhead Star Destroyer shot.

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:47.260
It’s an unspoken rule.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.790
It tells you everything you need to know instantly.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.149
The Empire is a looming presence.

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:56.399
Guaranteed this is how we’re going to begin
the Episode 7 movie too.

00:00:56.399 --> 00:01:00.380
Even in the expanded universe during the rise
of the New Republic, the Empire is still very

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:01.570
much a threat.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.359
The other really awesome thing about this
intro.

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:06.200
It’s quick and to the point.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.960
No foreplay.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.200
I totally love the title crawl, but if you
remember the family guy star wars episodes.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:18.030
It’s ripe for parody just because Too Long,
Didn’t Read.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:21.960
They’ll totally put it in Episode 7, the
movies are a much more appropriate place for

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:22.960
that kind of thing.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.329
Number 9 - Planet Lothal and the Outer Rim
Locations

00:01:26.329 --> 00:01:28.509
I was kind of glad they didn’t start on
Tatooine.

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:32.320
That’s been done enough, it’s a big Galaxy.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.619
And while Ezra is kind of a stand-in for young
Luke Skywalker, he’s not that character.

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:40.040
So putting it in a different part of the galaxy
helps distinguish the character.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.340
But yes, we were all thinking the same thing.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:48.289
Young Luke Skywalker meets a version of Obi-Wan
and gets swept up in an intergalactic adventure.

00:01:48.289 --> 00:01:52.180
There are only so many versions of the Hero’s
Journey Tale you can tell.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:55.180
Which is why I can’t wait for the Boba Fett
movie to come.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:02:01.750
That will be a very different spin on a Star
Wars story.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.640
Rebels is going to to travel all over the
Outer Rim, there will be a little overlap

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:08.679
with planets we saw in Clone Wars, like the
Kessel Spice Mines.

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:15.920
But the new series will take advantage of
some of the places we haven’t seen.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.580
It’s a new show so I’m totally looking
forward to seeing new planets.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.980
If any of you are new to the Star Wars comics,
the one’s that Marvel will be making, expect

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:27.410
them to visit some new places too.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.390
Number 8 - The Sound Design

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.030
The Star Wars Universe sounds very specific
and very different from other science fiction

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.130
places.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:39.280
Most other science fiction, not including
anime, actually steals a lot from Star Wars.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:45.010
Or I guess you would say is “Inspired by
Star Wars”

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:55.200
Everything from the different types of engine
sounds to blasters to doors opening and closing,

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.110
it instantly makes you feel at home.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.730
It’s all very familiar in a comfortable
way.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:04.290
In fact, a lot of the big action sequences
were sound mapped to sync up with the beats

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:09.160
in the original trilogy that inspired them,
like the speeder bike chase or the catwalk

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.740
scene from Empire Strikes Back.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.850
It reminds you of how important the technical
people on the production are.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:20.070
There’s an army of Sound Editors and engineers
that pick through thousands of sound effects

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.580
to add after all the voice over work is done
and the score is composed.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:27.320
The Score too, very awesome in the episode.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:30.370
It’s a modified version of the classic John
Williams score.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:33.940
I think that’s another law of Star Wars
productions.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:39.070
Anytime you make a new series, you have to
incorporate the Classic Williams score somehow.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.340
Number 7 - Team Ghost Rolls Out Central City

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:45.900
You can see from the non verbal way they pull
their heist that they’ve been doing this

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.100
together for a long time.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.640
They’re a strong team so the wild card is
always going to be Ezra.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:54.560
The heist itself doesn’t really go down
as planned, but I always love meeting teams

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.690
after they’ve come together.

00:03:56.690 --> 00:04:01.300
It’s a lot of fun to watch a bunch of strangers
get thrown together and try to figure things

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.300
out.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.310
But when that happens you have to hijack a
lot of your stories with exposition to show

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.170
them evolving as a group.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:10.920
Where we are in Rebels, the crew of the Ghost
is already at their peak.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:19.109
So now they can have more fun telling “mischief
managed” stories.

00:04:19.109 --> 00:04:21.129
Number 6 - The Ghost Ship

00:04:21.129 --> 00:04:24.990
Yes it is inspired by the Millenium Falcon,
technically it’s just a different smaller

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.699
model of Corellian Light Freighter.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:30.539
They haven’t revealed whether it’s been
modified as extensively as the Falcon.

00:04:30.539 --> 00:04:38.259
I 
love how the Corellian Freighter design has

00:04:38.259 --> 00:04:41.919
become synonymous with galactic piracy and
loveable scoundrels.

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:45.860
This is just the first episode so we’ll
see more of the ship in the future.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:49.389
But just looking at the state of things gives
you a good picture for how well the crew is

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.620
doing.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:53.879
The computer animation does a good job of
making everything feel dirty.

00:04:53.879 --> 00:04:58.070
One of the things I didn’t like as much
about the Clone Wars was all the surfaces

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:08.710
always looked brand new.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:16.419
It 
looks like they make just enough to get by,

00:05:16.419 --> 00:05:18.750
they’re not rolling in credits or anything.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:23.150
It gives the series a much greater sense of
urgency when your characters are always searching

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:25.110
for their next meal.

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:27.330
Number 5 - Obi Wan Kenobi Appearance

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:32.960
He’s not a main character on the show, but
the Holocron is a good device for future cameos.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:36.789
In terms of Clone Wars people, they have said
Ashoka and most of the other characters are

00:05:36.789 --> 00:05:40.070
still canon, so there is potential for them
to pop up.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:44.139
But mostly we’ll be focusing on all the
new people we met in this episode.

00:05:44.139 --> 00:05:46.199
Number 4 - The Kessel Fight

00:05:46.199 --> 00:05:49.340
It was a nice way to callback to the original
series and the Clone Wars.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:52.870
I know some of you were wondering who that
young wookie was supposed to be.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.900
It wasn’t chewbacca, in the canon chewbacca
is close to 200 years old at the beginning

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:58.590
of the original trilogy.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:02.879
As far as I know they haven’t changed that.

00:06:02.879 --> 00:06:09.650
I’m hoping that situations like this where
the Ghost saves groups of people gets paid

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:10.650
off later.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:15.150
Like the wookies helping them get out of a
jam later in the series.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:22.419
I didn’t think they were teasing any specific
characters with these wookies though.

00:06:22.419 --> 00:06:24.069
Number 3 - Agent Kallus

00:06:24.069 --> 00:06:28.090
One of my favorite new villains and one of
the smarter ones.

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:32.470
There’s this tendency to make villains on
children’s shows too silly.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:38.259
It’s done to show that the heroes will always
win.

00:06:38.259 --> 00:06:42.740
And yes, Rebels is a children’s show, but
that doesn’t mean that the crew of the Ghost

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:44.400
always has to win.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.240
You can still do a version of the downer ending
like Empire Strikes Back and have it be a

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.789
fun show.

00:06:50.789 --> 00:06:53.379
The Ezra prison block scene was a good example
of that.

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:57.729
He gets left behind, so the stakes go up and
when he’s rescued it’s a much more satisfying

00:06:57.729 --> 00:06:58.729
payoff.

00:06:58.729 --> 00:07:01.139
And it lets you know that Kallus isn’t completely
incompetent.

00:07:01.139 --> 00:07:07.440
He’s every bit as smart as anyone on the
ghost crew, so I think he’ll be one-upping

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.910
the ghost crew a lot this year.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:13.990
Number 2 - The Empire Strikes Back Catwalk
Rescue

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:17.060
The big payoff was Kanan rolling up on top
of the Ghost.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.370
Very Lando Calrissian of him.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:24.389
It would have been funny, but I am glad they
didn’t go for any “I am your father”

00:07:24.389 --> 00:07:25.389
references.

00:07:25.389 --> 00:07:26.389
That would have been a little too much.

00:07:26.389 --> 00:07:34.749
I totally loved the comedy, “First Jedi
you’ve ever seen sir?”

00:07:34.749 --> 00:07:37.360
and my number 1 moment - Meet the Inquisitor

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:42.150
Another great nod to Vader’s holo comm with
the Emperor in Empire.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:45.940
We’ll actually meet the Inqusitor in person
in the next couple of episodes.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:50.229
Some of the clips they’ve posted of him
fighting Kanan are from much later in the

00:07:50.229 --> 00:07:51.229
season though.

00:07:51.229 --> 00:07:53.370
I think this one is from episode 6.

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:57.800
He’s being voiced by Lucius Malfoy, which
is totally appropriate.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:02.089
Dave Filoni described him as an evil Sherlock
Holmes.

00:08:02.089 --> 00:08:05.550
When he said that I wondered why he didn’t
just say Moriarty.

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:10.220
But Moriarty and Sherlock aren’t perfect
copies of each other.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:12.229
Moriarty revels in chaos.

00:08:12.229 --> 00:08:15.819
So I think by calling the Inquisitor an evil
Sherlock, Filoni just means that he’s a

00:08:15.819 --> 00:08:18.240
genius detective that loves solving cases.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:22.919
He’s not out to burn down the galaxy or
mass murder civilians.

00:08:22.919 --> 00:08:25.349
Darth Vader gave him a case and he’s solving
it.

00:08:25.349 --> 00:08:27.210
One Jedi at a Time.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:37.870
We can talk more about him when he actually
shows up in an episode for real.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:40.700
Let me know what your favorite moment was.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:48.500
And which clone wars characters are you hoping
they bring on?

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:57.320
I guess as a bonus one of my favorites was
the Obi Wan Kenobi speech Kanan got at the

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:58.320
end.

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:02.070
I already talked a lot about it in my review
video so I didn’t want to repeat myself.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:06.370
My next Rebels video will be a bonus video
before the October 13th Episode.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.060
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:10.370
It’s going to be a Monday Show starting
October 13th and I’ll be doing videos for

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:11.370
all the episodes.

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:14.930
Because Gotham is also on Mondays my Rebels
videos will probably post Tuesday Mornings

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:15.930
pacific time.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:16.930
Let me know if there’s anything Rebels Specific
stuff you guys want to talk about and I’ll

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:17.990
add it to my list of bonus videos to do.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:22.190
Right now click here for my review of the
episode and click here for my Legend Of Korra

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:23.190
Episode 1 video.

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:25.470
Who else is happy that just came back too?

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:28.920
Thanks for watching everyone, now let’s
all high five and get ready for doctor who

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:29.310
tomorrow

